1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 { * Nimzo-Indian Defense. } 3. Nc3 Bb4 { [%cal Gb4e1] } 4. Nf3 b6 { Black tends to Fianchetto the light squared bishop, and later on bring a knight to e4. } { [%cal Gc8b7] } 5. e3 Bb7 6. Qc2 Ne4 { [%cal Ge4c3,Gb4c3] } 7. Bd3 f5! { This f5 move might seem bad at first but it helps defend black's powerful knight and prepares a very strong attack on the king side. } 8. O-O Nxc3 9. bxc3 Bxf3 10. gxf3 Be7 { Black is soon going to castle, and have a nice game. Though black didn't get an attack they sometimes have to be okay with that. In the next chapter There will be an example game, where black DOES get to attack with this opening. } *

